    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0693" n="677" sameAs="frus:frus1947v04/pg677"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/4–2547</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador of the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Novikov</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 60</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-04-25">April 25, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that I have
                    returned to Washington and, in accordance with the agreement reached between the
                    Governments of the U.S.S.R. and the U.S.A. in regard to the regularization <pb
                        facs="0694" n="678" xml:id="pg678"/> of Lend-Lease, I am ready to begin
                    negotiations on the subject.</p>
                <p>I should be grateful if you would communicate to me the desires of the Department
                    of State as to the organization of the negotiations.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d470-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>N. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Novikov</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d470-f1" n="1" xml:id="d470-f1-content">
                <p>In his acknowledgment of April 29, Acting Secretary Acheson “proposed that these
                    settlement negotiations be opened at a meeting between Your Excellency and Mr.
                    Willard L. Thorp, Assistant Secretary of State for Economic Affairs, at one
                    o’clock on Wednesday, April 30, 1947” at the Department of State
                    (861.24/4–2547)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
